It may be a mistake in the Ascension Guide. Here's a quotation from
Kevin/Dylan's tools spoiler (for 3.4.0, but probably still valid):

# An uncursed scroll of charging will add 5 to 14 charges, and then bring
# the marker to a minimum of 50 charges. A blessed scroll of charging will
# add 10 to 25 charges, and then bring the marker to a minimum of 50
# charges (75 if between 51 and 74).

So for nearly empty magic markers, an uncursed scroll is as good as a blessed
one. A blessed scroll is only good for getting a MM with 40-ish charges up to
75 (which is mainly useful for writing high-level spell books - for writing
scrolls, using all your charges first is more efficient, since MMs can't be
recharged more than once), or for adding a bit more charges to a MM already
well charged.

